  <data name="SettingsSwitchBackNote" xml:space="preserve"><value>You can switch back to the driver default here at any time.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsAfterDriverTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>After a driver update</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsAfterDriverDesc" xml:space="preserve"><value>A new driver throws away every compiled shader, so compiled games stutter again until they are rebuilt.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsAskMe" xml:space="preserve"><value>Ask me</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsAskMeSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>A notification offers Compile now, When idle, or Skip. Nothing starts on its own.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsAutoIdle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Automatically, only while the PC is idle</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsAutoIdleSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stops the moment you touch the mouse or keyboard and picks up where it left off.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsModeOff" xml:space="preserve"><value>Off</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsModeOffSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>Rebuild games yourself from the Library.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsPauseWhileGaming" xml:space="preserve"><value>Pause background compiling while another game is running</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsBackgroundThreads" xml:space="preserve"><value>Threads for background rebuilds</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsNvidiaAutoTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Auto Shader Compilation (NVIDIA beta)</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsNvidiaSysUtil" xml:space="preserve"><value>System utilization</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsNvidiaRecTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>We recommend enabling it</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsNvidiaRecMsg" xml:space="preserve"><value>A beta feature of the NVIDIA App: after a driver update it re-compiles the games you have already played. SCSKiller adds everything else, so both together are best. The overlap costs little: shaders NVIDIA already rebuilt take about 1 ms each here.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsPatreonTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Patreon and community database</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsPatreonDesc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Patreon supporters get the community shader hash database and beta and alpha builds. Sign in with the Patreon account you support SCSKiller with.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsPatreonSignIn" xml:space="preserve"><value>Sign in with Patreon</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsCancel" xml:space="preserve"><value>Cancel</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsBrowserPrompt" xml:space="preserve"><value>Finish signing in in your browser. Nothing else is needed here.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsSignedInTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Signed in with Patreon</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsRefreshStatus" xml:space="preserve"><value>Refresh status</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsSignOut" xml:space="preserve"><value>Sign out</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsSharingTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>You're in. Want to help improve the community shader hash database?</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsSharingMsg" xml:space="preserve"><value>Your game shader hashes are shared anonymously, never linked to your Patreon account.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsShareAnon" xml:space="preserve"><value>Share anonymously</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsNotNow" xml:space="preserve"><value>Not now</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsUpdateChannel" xml:space="preserve"><value>Update channel</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsBackToStable" xml:space="preserve"><value>Go back to stable now</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsDownloadHashes" xml:space="preserve"><value>Download shared shader hashes</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsDownloadHashesSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>Hashes other players recorded for your games, so they compile without you recording them first. No game files: your GPU compiles everything from your own install. Upscaler pipelines (FSR, XeSS) download for everyone, without it.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsShareHashes" xml:space="preserve"><value>Share anonymous shader hashes</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsShareHashesSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>Helps everyone get better coverage. Your recordings' upscaler pipelines (FSR, XeSS) also reach everyone with the same upscaler version. Never linked to your Patreon account; nothing else about your games leaves your PC. Free for everyone.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsQueueSpeedTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Compile speed when you run the queue</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsCompileThreads" xml:space="preserve"><value>Compile threads</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsMaxMemory" xml:space="preserve"><value>Maximum memory for compiling</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsMaximumMode" xml:space="preserve"><value>Maximum mode: also compile every shader pairing</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsMaximumModeSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>Seems to help most on AMD. Compiles take longer and use more disk space.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsBackgroundTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>In the background</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsStartWindows" xml:space="preserve"><value>Start SCSKiller when Windows starts</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsStartWindowsSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>It waits in the notification area, next to the clock, to offer a rebuild after a driver update.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsCloseQuits" xml:space="preserve"><value>Closing the window quits SCSKiller</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsCloseQuitsSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>A running compile finishes saving first, like Quit in the notification area. Off: closing the window keeps SCSKiller there; right-click its icon to quit.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsScanAtStart" xml:space="preserve"><value>Scan games when SCSKiller starts</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsScanAtStartSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>Reads again what changed in each game's folders. Off: the last list shows, and a game is read again when you refresh, when it exits, or when Steam or the Xbox app updates it.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsNotifyShaders" xml:space="preserve"><value>Notify me when games have new shaders to compile</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsNotifyShadersSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>A compiled game gains pipelines from its recording, the shared shader hashes or an SCSKiller update. You're told once, never while you play.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsDailyCheck" xml:space="preserve"><value>Send an anonymous daily check</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsDailyCheckSub" xml:space="preserve"><value>Counts active installs: once a day, the app's version and your GPU vendor, with no identifier. Nothing about your PC or games.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsRecordAllTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Record in all compatible games</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsRecordAllDesc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Adds a small d3d12.dll to games without anti-cheat to catch shaders the plan missed and time each frame, so the game page shows what stuttered. Frame times stay on this PC. Never used in anti-cheat games. Switch off to remove it from every game you haven't turned it on for yourself.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsRecordLimit" xml:space="preserve"><value>Recording limit per game</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsRecordLimitDesc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Counts the recording in the game's folder and SCSKiller's copy of it. At the limit the game plays as usual: new pipelines just aren't recorded.</value></data>
  <data name="SettingsSpaceByGame" xml:space="preserve"><value>Space by game</value></data>
